{
  "id": "me3qov5",
  "title": "Chapter 5: Output Devices",
  "order": 5,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "prai6t1",
      "content": "Output devices are hardware components that present processed data and information from the computer to the user in a human-readable form such as text, images, audio, or printed documents."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Output Devices",
          "value": "4 Main Types",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Printer Classes",
          "value": "Impact & Non-Impact",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Vector Output",
          "value": "Plotters",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Audio Device",
          "value": "Speakers",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "crez8dq"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpsl15j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.1 Monitor"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Monitors act as the primary visual display units delivering softcopy output.",
        "Printers generate hardcopy output and are broadly categorized into Impact and Non-Impact types.",
        "Plotters are specialized line-drawing output devices designed for high-resolution vector graphics and engineering prints.",
        "Speakers convert processed digital signals into audible sound output."
      ],
      "id": "0oghzrg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e15eemd",
      "content": "A monitor is the most common output device used to display visual information generated by a computer. It is also called a Visual Display Unit (VDU)."
    },
    {
      "id": "divrg0v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.1.1 Types of Monitors"
    },
    {
      "id": "6mrmujk",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Monitor Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Technology</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Features</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>CRT</p>",
            "<p>Cathode Ray Tube</p>",
            "<p>Bulky, heavy, consumes more power.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>LCD</p>",
            "<p>Liquid Crystal Display</p>",
            "<p>Flat screen, low power consumption.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>LED</p>",
            "<p>Light Emitting Diode</p>",
            "<p>Improved brightness and energy efficiency.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mlalswq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.1.2 Monitor Characteristics"
    },
    {
      "id": "rtmxz9t",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Resolution – Number of pixels displayed on the screen.",
        "Refresh Rate – Number of times the screen updates per second.",
        "Pixel – Smallest unit of a digital image.",
        "Aspect Ratio – Ratio of width to height of the display."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ih7ojh7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.2 Printer"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ygw56sk",
      "content": "A printer is an output device that produces a hard copy of digital documents on paper."
    },
    {
      "id": "wcxfx7m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.2.1 Types of Printers"
    },
    {
      "id": "xmqrz4d",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Printer Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Category</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dot Matrix Printer</p>",
            "<p>Impact</p>",
            "<p>Uses pins to strike ribbon and print characters.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Daisy Wheel Printer</p>",
            "<p>Impact</p>",
            "<p>Produces letter-quality text using wheel-shaped print head.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Line Printer</p>",
            "<p>Impact</p>",
            "<p>Prints one line at a time, used in large organizations.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Inkjet Printer</p>",
            "<p>Non-Impact</p>",
            "<p>Sprays tiny ink droplets onto paper.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Laser Printer</p>",
            "<p>Non-Impact</p>",
            "<p>Uses laser technology and toner for fast printing.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1ffozk7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.2.2 Impact vs Non-Impact Printers"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Impact Printers",
        "Non-Impact Printers"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Mechanism",
          "Direct physical contact with paper via striking pins/hammer",
          "Uses chemical, heat, or ink spraying techniques without contact"
        ],
        [
          "Examples",
          "Dot Matrix, Daisy Wheel, Line Printers",
          "Laser, Inkjet, Thermal Printers"
        ],
        [
          "Print Quality & Speed",
          "Lower resolution and slower speed",
          "Higher resolution and faster speed"
        ],
        [
          "Noise Level",
          "Noisy during operation",
          "Quiet/Silent operation"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "683y31m"
    },
    {
      "id": "r2quucv",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Impact Printer</p>",
            "<p>Non-Impact Printer</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Uses mechanical striking</p>",
            "<p>No physical striking</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Noisy</p>",
            "<p>Quiet</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Example: Dot Matrix</p>",
            "<p>Example: Laser Printer</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nd34xbr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.3 Plotter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "950udf6",
      "content": "A plotter is a specialized output device used to produce high-quality graphics and technical drawings."
    },
    {
      "id": "adq0m8p",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.3.1 Types of Plotters"
    },
    {
      "id": "dqt45oe",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Plotter Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Drum Plotter</p>",
            "<p>Paper moves around a rotating drum while pen draws images.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Flatbed Plotter</p>",
            "<p>Paper remains fixed while pen moves over the surface.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "31vjuvq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.4 Speaker"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Impact printers (e.g., Dot Matrix) physically strike the ribbon on paper, whereas Non-Impact printers (e.g., Laser, Inkjet) use non-contact methods.",
        "Plotters are specifically tested as the preferred output device for Computer-Aided Design (CAD) and high-quality vector blueprints.",
        "Distinguish clearly between softcopy output (Monitors, Speakers) and hardcopy output (Printers, Plotters)."
      ],
      "id": "88ez4qb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i1j4tv0",
      "content": "Speakers are output devices used to produce sound from a computer."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l0da7fm",
      "content": "Common Uses:"
    },
    {
      "id": "ezm89v4",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Music playback",
        "Video sound",
        "Voice communication",
        "Multimedia applications"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "qbcnmh9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.5 Important Exam Points"
    },
    {
      "id": "nv2x1bv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Monitor is also called VDU (Visual Display Unit).",
        "CRT stands for Cathode Ray Tube.",
        "LCD stands for Liquid Crystal Display.",
        "LED stands for Light Emitting Diode.",
        "Dot Matrix Printer is an impact printer.",
        "Laser Printer is a non-impact printer.",
        "Plotters are used for engineering and architectural drawings."
      ]
    }
  ],
